  "design_principles": [
    "One normalized Pattern algebra is shared by every owner.",
    "A Pattern evaluates its subject exactly once.",
    "Structural probes are pure, deterministic, nonconsuming, nonthrowing and nonsuspending.",
    "Bindings, moves, borrows and assignments publish through one failure-atomic logical commit.",
    "A failed probe or false guard publishes no partial binding, move, exclusive borrow, assignment or authority.",
    "Fixed products use Tuple identity; ordered residual decomposition uses an admitted Sequence descriptor.",
    "No syntax is interpreted differently from the runtime type of its subject.",
    "Preview syntax does not imply implementation or product support."
  ],
